# Use the template

Task-focused recipes for working with this project and its template. For the
reasoning behind the tools, see [Tools &amp; architecture](../explanation/tools.md).

## Generate a new project

This project was created this way (shown for reference). Replace `OWNER` with the
template's location.

```bash
uv tool install copier
copier copy --trust gh:OWNER/copier-python-template path/to/new-project
```

Answer the prompts (project name, package name, author, Python version, coding
agents, SQL, license). With `--trust`, Copier also runs `git init`, `uv sync`, and
installs the git hooks.

## Update this project from the template

When the template improves, pull the changes in:

```bash
just update        # = copier update --trust --skip-answered
```

Review the diff, resolve any conflicts, then commit.

## Run the day-to-day commands

```bash
just install     # create the venv, install deps + git hooks
just qa          # full gate: lint + type-check + tests
just test        # tests only (add a path: just test tests/test_smoke.py)
just format      # auto-format and auto-fix
just typecheck   # mypy
just docs        # serve the docs locally with live reload
just             # list every recipe
```

## Add or remove a dependency

```bash
uv add httpx                      # runtime dependency
uv add --group dev pytest-mock    # dev tooling
uv add --group docs mkdocs-glightbox  # docs tooling
uv remove httpx
```

`uv` updates `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` — commit both.

## Change the Python version

The version is pinned in several coordinated places, so the cleanest path is to
let Copier re-apply it consistently:

```bash
just update        # re-answer the "Python version" prompt
```

If you change it by hand instead, update all of: `.python-version`,
`requires-python` and `target-version` in `pyproject.toml`, `[tool.mypy]`
`python_version`, `[tool.pylint.main]` `py-version`, and
`default_language_version` in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`.

## Manage environment variables

```bash
cp .env.template .env   # then fill in real values
```

`.env` is git-ignored; never commit it. Document new variables in `.env.template`.

## Add a skill or agent guidance

- Add a reusable agent skill: create `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with `name` and
  `description` frontmatter, then the instructions.
- Change project-wide agent behavior: edit `AGENTS.md`.

## Build and publish the docs

```bash
just docs-build    # build the static site into ./site (fails on warnings)
```

Pushing to `main` triggers the `Docs` workflow, which runs `mkdocs gh-deploy` and
publishes to GitHub Pages.
